# Service-only secrets for auth-service.
#
# Only auth-service's code ever reads JWT_PRIVATE_KEY / JWT_REFRESH_SECRET
# (verified: grep across apps/ finds no other service touching them). They
# are kept OUT of the shared root .env on purpose so the other 4 services'
# processes never load the JWT signing key into memory at all — see
# .ai/memory/conventions.jsonl (2026-07-05,
# "env-centralization-tradeoff-analysis-and-env-example-rewrite").
#
# Copy to apps/auth-service/.env.secrets (gitignored) — this file already has
# a real local-dev keypair filled in (fine for this demo project: no real
# user data behind it; only CLOUD API keys — search-service's
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/GEMINI_API_KEY — are excluded from committed examples).
#
# Generate a fresh RSA keypair if you want your own:
#   openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:2048 | base64 -w 0
#   openssl pkey -pubout | base64 -w 0   (run against the private key above)
JWT_PRIVATE_
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=local-dev-jwt-refresh-secret-do-not-use-in-prod
